BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Nataraja Yoga
UID:event_316665554@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053356Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T103000
SUMMARY:Yoga Vinyasa Krama - Talasana Krama & Pranayama
DESCRIPTION:Nataraja School of Traditional Yoga\nAll Classes RSVP Only at 
 least 24hrs prior\n[[breathprayeryoga@protonmail.com](mailto:breathprayery
 oga@protonmail.com)]([mailto:breathprayeryoga@protonmail.com](http://mailt
 o:breathprayeryoga@protonmail.com/))\, 707-235-1413\n\\**For All Classes -
  Certain injuries & health issues may be contraindicated - Please contact 
 me if you have a concern*\n**Talasana Krama (Foundational Sequence) & Pran
 ayama**\n**Mondays 9-10:30am - Songbird Cotati - RSVP**\n**$25\, Discounte
 d Class Passes & Sliding Scale Available**\nFundamental practices for unde
 rstanding the holistic nature\, energetics and Sanskrit yoga philosophy gu
 iding the approach of this comprehensive system. Long time yoga practition
 ers as well as new students will benefit. Experience the distinction of th
 is system verses other modern yoga/vinyasa practices commonly taught & the
  traditional & precise use of ujjayi breath as it relates to the Sanskrit 
 parameters\, moving with the breath and the importance of the pause. Talas
 ana is a very unique & profound krama initiating & establishing "samasthit
 i"\, the steadiness and focus of mind\, balanced energy and steadiness of 
 body - with the two feet together\, moving from the center\, all the major
  joints and muscles of the body are exercised using arm and hand movements
 \, back bends\, side bends\, twists\, forward bends\, squats and balancing
  foot stretches. The fingers interlaced create a prana circuit as they com
 e together in the repetitive movement over the head. The breath specific m
 ovements stretch the diaphragm\, psoas\, massage the heart and internal or
 gans\, clear the lungs\, drain the lymphatic system\, stimulate the vagus 
 nerve and calm the mind. Energy is created along the spine and central ner
 vous system\, and is distributed throughout the nadis and into the entire 
 energy body. Regular practice of Talasana flowers into to ananta samapatti
  and understanding "stillness in movement".\nClass begins with Opening Man
 tras & Ding Namaskar (Devotional Salutation to the Directional Spheres wit
 h Breath & Mantra). Then moves to Tāĺāsana to Savasana then Seated Prā
 nāyāma (Yogic Breathing) including Morning Cleansing Kriyas\, Ujjayi\, N
 adi Shuddi\, Samantraka Prānāyāma\, Pratyahara\, Dharana. May include S
 pecific Mudra (Energetic Bodily Gestures).
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nataraja-school-of-traditional-yoga/e
 vents/316665554/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260922T161505Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T161505Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Nataraja Yoga
UID:event_316710722@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053356Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T103000
SUMMARY:Yoga Vinyasa & Pranayama
DESCRIPTION:Nataraja School of Traditional Yoga\n**Yoga Vinyasa Krama - Th
 ursdays 9-10:30am**\n**Songbird Community Healing Center Cotati**\n**RSVP 
 ONLY**\nPhysical Health\, Conditioning\, Pranic Flow\, Vital Energy\, Ment
 al Focus & Stillness - through intelligent architecture with the metaphysi
 cs of deep conscious breathing & slow motion\, yogic breathwork\, mantra/s
 ound/vibration\, mudra\, subtle & contemplative practices.\nYoga Vinyasa K
 rama is a comprehensive hatha-raja yogic system for purification\, develop
 ing concentration\, neuromuscular fitness and conditioning\, refining & ma
 stering the breath\, awakening subtle energy and stilling the mind. Based 
 on deep breathing & the subtle movement of prana directed into the cartila
 ge tissue\, sinuous musculature\, internal organs\, nerve pathways and nad
 is. It has over 700 intelligently sequenced slow\, conscious breath powere
 d with precision movement variations with pause (vinyasas)\, exploring man
 y aesthetic variations of each posture to correctly establish the main asa
 nas while the mind merges with the breath.\nIncludes the energetics of dri
 shti\, pratikriyas\, bandha\, vaseth\, mudra\, mantra\, surya & ding namas
 kar with breath & mantra\, cleansing kriyas\, Himalayan pranayama includin
 g including ujjayi variations\, heating & cooling breaths\, solar\, lunar 
 & soli-lunar nadi shuddhi practices\, pranava & samantraka pranayama\, pra
 tyahara\, subtle & contemplative practices in 12 kramas (sequences).\nThe 
 whole process gradually transforms the body and mind\, releasing old patte
 rns of physical and mental tension and dysfunctional patterns of movement\
 , providing tonic\, energetic and psychophysiological effects.\nThis syste
 m is presented from the teachings **Srivatsa Ramaswami** learned through h
 is over 33 years of one on one study with **Sri Krishnamacharya** and teac
 hings from a similar **Himalayan method**.\nThis ongoing class will explor
 e the entire system of 12 Kramas with each class focusing on a particular 
 krama or vinyasas from different kramas & pranayama & dharana practices.\n
 Please practice on an empty stomach. Morning beverage ok but please take i
 t 30min or more before class.\n***Certain injuries & health issues may be 
 contraindicated Please contact me if you have a concern***\nKnowledge of U
 jjayi Breathing recommended\n**$25 Drop In\, Discounted Class Passes\, Sli
 ding Scale Available**\n\\*\\***RSVP Only** Contact Kara @707-235-1413\, [
 breathprayeryoga@protonmail.com](http://sunyogadance@gmail.com%2A%2A/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nataraja-school-of-traditional-yoga/e
 vents/316710722/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260925T160508Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T160508Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
